 action."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/OctanePacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OctanePacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/OctaneAsyncBatcherOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OctaneAsyncBatcherOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", {\n}>>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"code","value":"(item): Promise<any>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adds an item to the async batcher\nIf the batch size is reached, timeout occurs, or shouldProcess returns true, the batch will be processed"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"item","children":[{"type":"text","value":"item"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The result from the batch function, or undefined if an error occurred and was handled by onError"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"throws","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throws"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The error from the batch function if no onError handler is configured or throwOnError is true"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useAsyncBatchedCallback } from '@tanstack/octane-pacer'\n\n// During component rendering:\nconst schedule = useAsyncBatchedCallback(async (items: Array<number>) => { console.log(items) }, { maxSize: 5, wait: 500 })\nvoid schedule(1)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useAsyncBatcher"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"return-value","text":"Return value","level":2},{"id":"state-and-ownership","text":"State and ownership","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":3},{"id":"item","text":"item","level":4},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":3},{"id":"throws","text":"Throws","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncBatchedCallback<TValue>(fn, options): (item) => Promise<any>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-batcher/useAsyncBatchedCallback.ts:36](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/octane-pacer/src/async-batcher/useAsyncBatchedCallback.ts#L36)\n\nReturns a stable batched callback owned by the Octane lifecycle.\n\nCollects items until maxSize, wait, or getShouldExecute triggers a batch. Each call adds one item; the wrapped function receives an array.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns the bound addItem method, which accepts one item per call. The returned Promise preserves the core result and error contract. An addition that only schedules a batch does not await the later batch result.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nUse useAsyncBatcher when you need selected state or control methods. This callback does not expose the utility, its store, or a child subscription.\n\nCall during component rendering. The hook retains its utility across renders and runs cleanup when the component unmounts.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`items`) => `Promise`\\<`any`\\>\n\n### options\n\n[`OctanePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/OctanePacerOptions.md)\\<[`OctaneAsyncBatcherOptions`](../interfaces/OctaneAsyncBatcherOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, \\{\n\\}\\>\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n```ts\n(item): Promise<any>;\n```\n\nAdds an item to the async batcher\nIf the batch size is reached, timeout occurs, or shouldProcess returns true, the batch will be processed\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### item\n\n`TValue`\n\n### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`any`\\>\n\nThe result from the batch function, or undefined if an error occurred and was handled by onError\n\n### Throws\n\nThe error from the batch function if no onError handler is configured or throwOnError is true\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { useAsyncBatchedCallback } from '@tanstack/octane-pacer'\n\n// During component rendering:\nconst schedule = useAsyncBatchedCallback(async (items: Array<number>) => { console.log(items) }, { maxSize: 5, wait: 500 })\nvoid schedule(1)\n```\n\n## See\n\nuseAsyncBatcher\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useAsyncBatchedCallback\ntitle: useAsyncBatchedCallback\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncBatchedCallback<TValue>(fn, options): (item) => Promise<any>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-batcher/useAsyncBatchedCallback.ts:36](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/octane-pacer/src/async-batcher/useAsyncBatchedCallback.ts#L36)\n\nReturns a stable batched callback owned by the Octane lifecycle.\n\nCollects items until maxSize, wait, or getShouldExecute triggers a batch. Each call adds one item; the wrapped function receives an array.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns the bound addItem method, which accepts one item per call. The returned Promise preserves the core result and error contract. An addition that only schedules a batch does not await the later batch result.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nUse useAsyncBatcher when you need selected state or control methods. This callback does not expose the utility, its store, or a child subscription.\n\nCall during component rendering. The hook retains its utility across renders and runs cleanup when the component unmounts.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`items`) => `Promise`\\<`any`\\>\n\n### options\n\n[`OctanePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/OctanePacerOptions.md)\\<[`OctaneAsyncBatcherOptions`](../interfaces/OctaneAsyncBatcherOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, \\{\n\\}\\>\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n```ts\n(item): Promise<any>;\n```\n\nAdds an item to the async batcher\nIf the batch size is reached, timeout occurs, or shouldProcess returns true, the batch will be processed\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### item\n\n`TValue`\n\n### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`any`\\>\n\nThe result from the batch function, or undefined if an error occurred and was handled by onError\n\n### Throws\n\nThe error from the batch function if no onError handler is configured or throwOnError is true\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { useAsyncBatchedCallback } from '@tanstack/octane-pacer'\n\n// During component rendering:\nconst schedule = useAsyncBatchedCallback(async (items: Array<number>) => { console.log(items) }, { maxSize: 5, wait: 500 })\nvoid schedule(1)\n```\n\n## See\n\nuseAsyncBatcher\n"}
